"Sigilian" by Anonymous

The story headline is "An Interactive Fiction".
The story genre is "Fantasy".
The release number is 1.

When play begins:
	say "You surface slowly from the deep waters of sleep, consciousness returning in fragments. The air is cool against your skin. Somewhere nearby, the faint scent of dust and old stone lingers.[paragraph break]Your body feels heavy, unwilling to move. The mattress beneath you is thin but familiar — you have slept here before, though the memory of how you arrived escapes you.[paragraph break]You open your eyes."

Chapter 1 - The Starting Room

The Cell is a room. "A small, spare room of grey stone. A narrow window set high in the wall admits a shaft of pale light that falls across the floor. The walls are bare except for a series of faint scratches near the door — tally marks, perhaps, though you cannot be sure. The air is still and carries a faint chill."

The bed is an enterable supporter in the Cell. "A simple wooden bed frame stands against the far wall, its thin mattress slightly rumpled." The description of the bed is "A narrow bed with a plain wooden frame. The mattress is thin and coarse, the sort of thing that leaves you stiff in the morning. A single wool blanket lies bunched at the foot."

The blanket is on the bed. The description of the blanket is "A rough wool blanket, grey and threadbare in places. It smells faintly of dust."

The player is on the bed.

The narrow window is scenery in the Cell. The description of the narrow window is "A slit of a window, too high and too narrow to climb through. Through it you can see only a rectangle of pale sky."

The tally marks are scenery in the Cell. The description of the tally marks is "Groups of five, scratched into the stone with something sharp. You count them: forty-seven days. Or perhaps someone simply lost count."

The door is scenery in the Cell. The description of the door is "A heavy wooden door banded with iron. It is shut fast."

Instead of opening the door, say "It won't budge. Locked from the outside."
